.TH SDL_DestroyWindow 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_DestroyWindow \- Destroy a window.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_DestroyWindow(SDL_Window *window);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Any child windows owned by the window will be recursively destroyed as well\[char46]
.PP
Note that on some platforms, the visible window may not actually be removed from the screen until the SDL event loop is pumped again, even though the
.BR SDL_Window
is no longer valid after this call\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to destroy\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

